\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If every positive element of a complex C*-algebra is properly infinite in Cuntz comparison, must the algebra be strongly purely infinite, with simultaneous two-element diagonalization, without exactness, nuclearity, unitality or simplicity assumptions?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If every positive element of a complex C*-algebra is properly infinite in Cuntz comparison, must the algebra be strongly purely infinite, with simultaneous two-element diagonalization, without exactness, nuclearity, unitality or simplicity assumptions?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Weak-pure-infiniteness-and-O-infinity-absorption-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

